- logic errors in fee calculation, transaction assembly, or UTXO selection;
- parsing or validation errors in network responses, addresses, scripts,
  transactions, or user input;
- concurrency or state-handling errors in multi-step operations (scan,
  build, broadcast);
- security vulnerabilities that could allow unauthorized access to funds,
  secrets, or device;
- silent failure modes that cause incorrect results without error indication;
- errors that only manifest under specific timing, network, or hardware
